[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Real vector echo substitution

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Bounded repair to the existing reporting evaluator. Reuse decision: retain
string.Join and the existing finite-vector validator and numeric formatter;
no parser, interpreter or dependency is added. The pinned RSpice source
29c28a022625fd7cc2c56ead1cce2d3066663074 documents vector_words in
crates/rspice-core-netlist/src/control_protocol.rs and expand_vector in
crates/rspice-core/src/engine/control/presentation/vectors.rs: $& produces
one word per vector element. Source was consulted as behavioral guidance;
no RSpice source was copied. The independent stock ngspice executable and
unchanged regression/model/special-names-1.cir provide execution evidence.
This repair changes real echo cardinality; existing complex formatting and
unsupported indexed substitutions retain their established contracts.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-REAL-VECTOR-ECHO-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Complete bounded real vector echo substitution
STATEMENT: >>>
For an admitted echo command, $&name shall substitute every finite component
of the named real vector in original order, separated by spaces, using the
existing invariant numeric formatter. A scalar shall remain one word.
Evaluation shall not mutate borrowed input vectors. Unknown names, unsupported
indexed or member substitutions, empty vectors and vectors exceeding 4096
components shall fail without publishing partial report output.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.Syntax/ControlVectorExecution.cs.
Verification: dotnet/Simulator.Syntax.Tests/VectorEchoTests.cs; unchanged
original regression/model/special-names-1.cir, complete reporting/assertions
and all nine mapped OP voltage/current observables against default ngspice.
Evidence: evidence/real-vector-echo.json and docs/real-vector-echo-results.md.
Draft status does not claim broad control-language or text-format parity.
<<<
